Rem ==================================================================
Rem html.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: HTML, forgivingly
Rem
Rem A reader and a writer for HTML, built on xml.shoddy. A parsed page
Rem IS an Xml tree — the same XElem, XText, XComment and XDoctype — so
Rem every word xml already has works on it unchanged:
Rem
Rem     Let page = HtmlLoad("index.html")
Rem     Print(XTextOf(XFind(page, "title")))
Rem     Print(Length(HLinks(page)))
Rem     Print(XAttrOr(HById(page, "main"), "class", ""))
Rem
Rem That is the whole design. html adds a reader that tolerates what
Rem real pages do, a writer that knows HTML is not XML, an entity table
Rem and a few conveniences. Navigation, construction and equality are
Rem xml's and are not written twice.
Rem
Rem     HtmlParse / HtmlRead      HById / HByIdOr
Rem     HtmlText / HtmlPretty     HTitle / HTitleOr
Rem
Rem ---- WHAT THIS IS NOT --------------------------------------------
Rem
Rem This is a FORGIVING TAG-SOUP READER, not an HTML5 parser, and the
Rem difference is not a formality. HTML5 specifies a tree-construction
Rem algorithm — the stack of open elements, the list of active
Rem formatting elements, the adoption agency, foster parenting, the
Rem twenty-odd insertion modes — that exists to make every browser agree
Rem on what a broken page means. None of that is here.
Rem
Rem What that costs you, concretely. Misnested formatting is not
Rem repaired: <b><i>x</b></i> does not come back as the two overlapping
Rem runs a browser would build. A <tbody> a browser would invent around
Rem your rows is not invented. Content that HTML5 would move out of a
Rem table and place before it is left where it was written. A page that
Rem relies on any of that will parse — this reader does not abort easily
Rem — but the tree will be the one the bytes describe, not the one the
Rem browser shows.
Rem
Rem What IS handled, because real hand-written pages are full of it:
Rem tag and attribute names folded to lower case; the fifteen void
Rem elements, closed or not; raw-text elements, so a < inside <script>
Rem or <style> is not markup; unquoted, single-quoted and valueless
Rem attributes; comments and the doctype; end tags implied by a sibling
Rem or a closing parent, for the elements that customarily omit them;
Rem and an end tag that closes something other than the innermost open
Rem element, which closes everything up to it rather than failing.
Rem
Rem ---- entities ----------------------------------------------------
Rem
Rem HTML5 names 2231 character references. This table holds the ones
Rem that appear in hand-written pages — the arrows, dashes, quotes and
Rem symbols — plus numeric references in either base. An unknown name is
Rem left standing as its own text, exactly as a browser leaves it, and
Rem is never an error: refusing to render a page over one bad ampersand
Rem is the behaviour HTML spent thirty years getting rid of.
Rem
Rem &#0; is the exception, and it is xml's exception too: Chr(0) is the
Rem empty string in Shoddy, so it is left standing rather than silently
Rem shortening the text.
Rem
Rem ---- other limits ------------------------------------------------
Rem
Rem The bytes are someone else's problem. ReadFile decides how the file
Rem became a string; a <meta charset> is read as an ordinary element and
Rem changes nothing.
Rem
Rem Text is decoded, so a round trip is CANONICAL rather than literal,
Rem as it is in xml: &mdash; comes back as the character itself, an
Rem unquoted attribute comes back quoted, and a void element comes back
Rem in the bare form. HtmlText is a fixed point from the first write on.
Rem
Rem Compare with XEqual, not with =, for the same reason xml says so.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "xml.shoddy"

Rem ---- constants -------------------------------------------------------
Rem Machines cannot carry a top-level Let, so the tables are zero-arg
Rem Defs, as vt100's Esc() is.

Rem The void elements: they have no content and no end tag. Written
Rem bare — <br>, not <br/> — because that is what HTML5 serialises and
Rem what every page in the wild contains.
Def HVoids() As List Of String
    { "area", "base", "br", "col", "embed", "hr", "img", "input", "link", "meta", "param", "source", "track", "wbr" }

Rem Inside these, < does not start a tag. Everything up to the matching
Rem end tag is text, which is the only way a page can carry JavaScript
Rem containing a < without escaping it.
Def HRawText() As List Of String
    { "script", "style" }

Rem What closes an open element when it starts. The list is the
Rem customary one; it is what makes a page written without </li> parse
Rem into the list the author meant. Note that a cell is closed by the
Rem next ROW as well as by the next cell — without that, a table written
Rem without a single end tag nests one row inside the last cell of the
Rem one before it, which is the shape of a great many hand-written pages.
Def HClosedBySibling() As List Of Pair
    { Pair("li", { "li" }), Pair("dt", { "dt", "dd" }), Pair("dd", { "dd", "dt" }),
      Pair("option", { "option" }), Pair("tr", { "tr" }),
      Pair("td", { "td", "th", "tr" }), Pair("th", { "th", "td", "tr" }),
      Pair("thead", { "tbody", "tfoot" }), Pair("tbody", { "tbody", "tfoot" }), Pair("tfoot", { "tbody" }) }

Rem A <p> also closes when any of these opens, because none of them can
Rem be inside a paragraph.
Def HClosesP() As List Of String
    { "address", "article", "aside", "blockquote", "div", "dl", "fieldset", "footer", "form", "h1", "h2", "h3", "h4", "h5", "h6", "header", "hr", "main", "nav", "ol", "p", "pre", "section", "table", "ul" }

Rem The named character references worth carrying. Chosen by counting
Rem what hand-written pages actually use rather than by transcribing the
Rem HTML5 table: the five XML predefines, the spaces and dashes, the
Rem quotes, the arrows, and the handful of symbols and letters that turn
Rem up in ordinary prose. Anything else is left as its own text.
Rem
Rem The values are XUtf8, not Chr, and xml.shoddy explains at length why:
Rem ReadFile is one byte to one character, so &mdash; has to decode to
Rem the same three bytes a literal em dash in the file already is.
Def HEntities() As List Of Pair
    { Pair("amp", "&"), Pair("lt", "<"), Pair("gt", ">"), Pair("quot", XUtf8(34)), Pair("apos", XUtf8(39)),
      Pair("nbsp", XUtf8(160)), Pair("ensp", XUtf8(8194)), Pair("emsp", XUtf8(8195)), Pair("thinsp", XUtf8(8201)),
      Pair("shy", XUtf8(173)), Pair("ndash", XUtf8(8211)), Pair("mdash", XUtf8(8212)), Pair("minus", XUtf8(8722)),
      Pair("lsquo", XUtf8(8216)), Pair("rsquo", XUtf8(8217)), Pair("ldquo", XUtf8(8220)), Pair("rdquo", XUtf8(8221)),
      Pair("laquo", XUtf8(171)), Pair("raquo", XUtf8(187)), Pair("hellip", XUtf8(8230)), Pair("middot", XUtf8(183)),
      Pair("bull", XUtf8(8226)), Pair("dagger", XUtf8(8224)), Pair("Dagger", XUtf8(8225)), Pair("prime", XUtf8(8242)),
      Pair("larr", XUtf8(8592)), Pair("uarr", XUtf8(8593)), Pair("rarr", XUtf8(8594)), Pair("darr", XUtf8(8595)),
      Pair("harr", XUtf8(8596)), Pair("lArr", XUtf8(8656)), Pair("rArr", XUtf8(8658)), Pair("hArr", XUtf8(8660)),
      Pair("copy", XUtf8(169)), Pair("reg", XUtf8(174)), Pair("trade", XUtf8(8482)), Pair("deg", XUtf8(176)),
      Pair("times", XUtf8(215)), Pair("divide", XUtf8(247)), Pair("plusmn", XUtf8(177)), Pair("frac12", XUtf8(189)),
      Pair("frac14", XUtf8(188)), Pair("frac34", XUtf8(190)), Pair("sup1", XUtf8(185)), Pair("sup2", XUtf8(178)),
      Pair("sup3", XUtf8(179)), Pair("micro", XUtf8(181)), Pair("para", XUtf8(182)), Pair("sect", XUtf8(167)),
      Pair("pound", XUtf8(163)), Pair("euro", XUtf8(8364)), Pair("yen", XUtf8(165)), Pair("cent", XUtf8(162)),
      Pair("dollar", "$"), Pair("permil", XUtf8(8240)), Pair("infin", XUtf8(8734)), Pair("ne", XUtf8(8800)),
      Pair("le", XUtf8(8804)), Pair("ge", XUtf8(8805)), Pair("asymp", XUtf8(8776)), Pair("equiv", XUtf8(8801)),
      Pair("alpha", XUtf8(945)), Pair("beta", XUtf8(946)), Pair("gamma", XUtf8(947)), Pair("delta", XUtf8(948)),
      Pair("pi", XUtf8(960)), Pair("sigma", XUtf8(963)), Pair("mu", XUtf8(956)), Pair("lambda", XUtf8(955)),
      Pair("Omega", XUtf8(937)), Pair("agrave", XUtf8(224)), Pair("aacute", XUtf8(225)), Pair("eacute", XUtf8(233)),
      Pair("egrave", XUtf8(232)), Pair("iacute", XUtf8(237)), Pair("oacute", XUtf8(243)), Pair("uacute", XUtf8(250)),
      Pair("ouml", XUtf8(246)), Pair("auml", XUtf8(228)), Pair("uuml", XUtf8(252)), Pair("ccedil", XUtf8(231)),
      Pair("ntilde", XUtf8(241)), Pair("szlig", XUtf8(223)), Pair("oslash", XUtf8(248)), Pair("aring", XUtf8(229)) }

Def HIsVoid(tag As String) As Boolean
    Contains(HVoids(), Lower(tag))

Def HIsRawText(tag As String) As Boolean
    Contains(HRawText(), Lower(tag))

Rem ======================================================================
Rem THE READER
Rem ======================================================================
Rem The shape is xml's — every step returns the node it built and the
Rem index of the next unconsumed character, or why and where it gave up —
Rem but the rules are HTML's, and the interesting difference is that an
Rem end tag which does not match can CLOSE the open element rather than
Rem fail. That is what the pending flag threads through the child loop:
Rem when a step stops because it met an end tag belonging to an ancestor,
Rem it leaves the index pointing AT that end tag for the ancestor to
Rem deal with.

Rem ---- entities --------------------------------------------------------
Rem HTML's rules are laxer than XML's: an ampersand that does not begin a
Rem reference we know is simply an ampersand.

Def HEntLen(s As String, i As Number) As Number
    Let e = XEntEnd(s, i)
    If e = 0 Then
        0
    Else
        Let name = Mid(s, i + 1, e - i - 1)
        If HEntText(name) = "" Then
            0
        Else
            e - i + 1

Rem The text a name stands for, or "" if this table does not know it.
Rem The numeric forms are xml's, so &#0; is refused here too.
Def HEntText(name As String) As String
    If DictHas(HEntities(), name) Then
        DictGet(HEntities(), name)
    Else
        If XEntCode(name) > 0 Then
            XUtf8(XEntCode(name))
        Else
            ""

Rem The public spelling: the text a reference stands for, with the
Rem ampersand and semicolon included, or "" if it is not one we know.
Def HtmlEntity(name As String) As String
    HEntText(name)

Rem ---- text ------------------------------------------------------------

Def HTextAt(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    HTextBody(s, i, i, { })

Def HTextBody(s As String, i As Number, run As Number, acc As List Of String) As XTake
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XTook(XText(Join(Reverse(XRun(s, run, i, acc)), "")), i)
    Else
        Let c = Mid(s, i, 1)
        If c = "<" Then
            XTook(XText(Join(Reverse(XRun(s, run, i, acc)), "")), i)
        Else
            If c = "&" And HEntLen(s, i) > 0 Then
                HTextBody(s, i + HEntLen(s, i), i + HEntLen(s, i), Prepend(HEntText(Mid(s, i + 1, HEntLen(s, i) - 2)), XRun(s, run, i, acc)))
            Else
                HTextBody(s, i + 1, run, acc)

Rem Everything up to the matching end tag, verbatim. No entity is
Rem decoded and no < is markup, which is what <script> requires.
Def HRawAt(s As String, i As Number, tag As String) As XTake
    Let e = HFindClose(s, i, tag)
    If e = 0 Then
        XTook(XText(Mid(s, i, Len(s) - i + 1)), Len(s) + 1)
    Else
        XTook(XText(Mid(s, i, e - i)), e)

Rem The index of </tag, case-insensitively, at or after i. Lower-cases
Rem only the tail it is searching, which is bounded by the document.
Def HFindClose(s As String, i As Number, tag As String) As Number
    If i > Len(s) Then
        0
    Else
        Let p = Instr(Lower(Mid(s, i, Len(s) - i + 1)), "</" & Lower(tag))
        If p = 0 Then
            0
        Else
            i + p - 1

Rem ---- attributes ------------------------------------------------------
Rem Three spellings are allowed where XML allows one: quoted with either
Rem quote, unquoted up to the next whitespace or >, and bare — a name
Rem with no value at all, which HTML gives the empty string.

Def HIsAttrNameChar(c As String) As Boolean
    If Len(c) <> 1 Then
        False
    Else
        Not (XIsWs(c) Or c = "=" Or c = ">" Or c = "/" Or c = XQt() Or c = XAp())

Def HAttrNameEnd(s As String, i As Number) As Number
    If HIsAttrNameChar(Mid(s, i, 1)) Then
        HAttrNameEnd(s, i + 1)
    Else
        i

Def HUnquotedEnd(s As String, i As Number) As Number
    Let c = Mid(s, i, 1)
    If Len(c) = 0 Or XIsWs(c) Or c = ">" Then
        i
    Else
        HUnquotedEnd(s, i + 1)

Rem A quoted value, decoded with HTML's entity rules.
Def HQuotedValue(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    HQuotedBody(s, i + 1, i + 1, Mid(s, i, 1), { })

Def HQuotedBody(s As String, i As Number, run As Number, q As String, acc As List Of String) As XTake
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XTook(XText(Join(Reverse(XRun(s, run, i, acc)), "")), i)
    Else
        Let c = Mid(s, i, 1)
        If c = q Then
            XTook(XText(Join(Reverse(XRun(s, run, i, acc)), "")), i + 1)
        Else
            If c = "&" And HEntLen(s, i) > 0 Then
                HQuotedBody(s, i + HEntLen(s, i), i + HEntLen(s, i), q, Prepend(HEntText(Mid(s, i + 1, HEntLen(s, i) - 2)), XRun(s, run, i, acc)))
            Else
                HQuotedBody(s, i + 1, run, q, acc)

Rem The attributes of a start tag, gathered until > or />. Handed back
Rem inside a nameless XElem, which is the only way to return a
Rem List Of Pair through an XTake — the same trick xml uses.
Def HAttrsAt(s As String, i As Number, acc As List Of Pair) As XTake
    Let k = XSkipWs(s, i)
    If k > Len(s) Then
        XTook(XElem("", Reverse(acc), { }), k)
    Else
        Let c = Mid(s, k, 1)
        If c = ">" Or Mid(s, k, 2) = "/>" Then
            XTook(XElem("", Reverse(acc), { }), k)
        Else
            If c = "/" Or Not HIsAttrNameChar(c) Then
                HAttrsAt(s, k + 1, acc)
            Else
                Let n = HAttrNameEnd(s, k)
                Let name = Lower(Mid(s, k, n - k))
                Let eq = XSkipWs(s, n)
                If Mid(s, eq, 1) <> "=" Then
                    HAttrsAt(s, n, HPutFirst(acc, name, ""))
                Else
                    Let v = XSkipWs(s, eq + 1)
                    Let vc = Mid(s, v, 1)
                    If vc = XQt() Or vc = XAp() Then
                        Select Case HQuotedValue(s, v)
                            Case XTook(XText(val), n2)
                                HAttrsAt(s, n2, HPutFirst(acc, name, val))
                            Case Else
                                HAttrsAt(s, v + 1, acc)
                    Else
                        Let ue = HUnquotedEnd(s, v)
                        HAttrsAt(s, ue, HPutFirst(acc, name, HtmlUnescape(Mid(s, v, ue - v))))

Rem HTML keeps the FIRST of a repeated attribute and ignores the rest,
Rem which is the opposite of what an object literal does in json. The
Rem accumulator is reversed at the end, so "already present" is the test.
Def HPutFirst(acc As List Of Pair, name As String, val As String) As List Of Pair
    If DictHas(acc, name) Then
        acc
    Else
        Prepend(Pair(name, val), acc)

Rem ---- elements --------------------------------------------------------

Rem Does an open <cur> end because <starting> is starting?
Def HImpliedBySibling(cur As String, starting As String) As Boolean
    If cur = "p" Then
        Contains(HClosesP(), starting)
    Else
        If DictHas(HClosedBySibling(), cur) Then
            Contains(DictGet(HClosedBySibling(), cur), starting)
        Else
            False

Rem The element at i, and everything under it. Returns the index just
Rem past its end tag, or — when it ended because an ancestor's end tag
Rem or an implying sibling arrived — the index AT whatever ended it, for
Rem the caller to look at again.
Def HElemAt(s As String, i As Number, d As Number, stack As List Of String) As XTake
    If d <= 0 Then
        XTBad("NESTING TOO DEEP", i)
    Else
        Let n = HAttrNameEnd(s, i + 1)
        If n = i + 1 Then
            XTook(XText("<"), i + 1)
        Else
            Let tag = Lower(Mid(s, i + 1, n - i - 1))
            Select Case HAttrsAt(s, n, { })
                Case XTook(XElem(ignored, attrs, unused), k)
                    HElemBody(s, HTagEnd(s, k), d, tag, attrs, Mid(s, k, 2) = "/>", stack)
                Case Else
                    XTBad("EXPECTED A START TAG", i)

Rem The index just past the > that ends a start tag.
Def HTagEnd(s As String, k As Number) As Number
    If Mid(s, k, 2) = "/>" Then
        k + 2
    Else
        If Mid(s, k, 1) = ">" Then
            k + 1
        Else
            k

Def HElemBody(s As String, i As Number, d As Number, tag As String, attrs As List Of Pair, selfClosed As Boolean, stack As List Of String) As XTake
    If HIsVoid(tag) Or selfClosed Then
        XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, { }), i)
    Else
        If HIsRawText(tag) Then
            Select Case HRawAt(s, i, tag)
                Case XTook(XText(raw), e)
                    XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, HRawKids(raw)), HSkipEndTag(s, e, tag))
                Case Else
                    XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, { }), i)
        Else
            HKidsAt(s, i, d, tag, attrs, { }, Prepend(tag, stack))

Rem An empty raw-text element has no text child rather than an empty one.
Def HRawKids(raw As String) As List Of Xml
    If raw = "" Then
        { }
    Else
        { XText(raw) }

Rem Step over </tag ... > if it is there.
Def HSkipEndTag(s As String, i As Number, tag As String) As Number
    If Mid(s, i, 2) <> "</" Then
        i
    Else
        Let g = XInstrFrom(s, i, ">")
        If g = 0 Then
            Len(s) + 1
        Else
            g + 1

Rem The stack is the elements open around and including this one, which
Rem is what makes the difference between an end tag that belongs to an
Rem ancestor and one that belongs to nobody. The first closes everything
Rem down to its owner; the second is DROPPED. Without the stack the two
Rem are indistinguishable, and a stray </p> left over from a paragraph
Rem that some other rule already closed tears the rest of the page off
Rem the tree.
Def HKidsAt(s As String, i As Number, d As Number, tag As String, attrs As List Of Pair, acc As List Of Xml, stack As List Of String) As XTake
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, Reverse(acc)), i)
    Else
        If Mid(s, i, 2) = "</" Then
            Let n = HAttrNameEnd(s, i + 2)
            Let close = Lower(Mid(s, i + 2, n - i - 2))
            If close = tag Then
                XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, Reverse(acc)), HSkipEndTag(s, i, tag))
            Else
                If Contains(stack, close) Then
                    Rem An ancestor's. Close here and leave the index AT
                    Rem it, for the ancestor to find.
                    XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, Reverse(acc)), i)
                Else
                    Rem Nobody's. Step over it and carry on.
                    HKidsAt(s, HSkipEndTag(s, i, close), d, tag, attrs, acc, stack)
        Else
            If HStartsElem(s, i) And HImpliedBySibling(tag, HTagAt(s, i)) Then
                XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, Reverse(acc)), i)
            Else
                Select Case HNodeAt(s, i, d - 1, stack)
                    Case XTBad(why, at)
                        XTBad(why, at)
                    Case XTook(v, n)
                        If n <= i Then
                            XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, Reverse(acc)), Len(s) + 1)
                        Else
                            HKidsAt(s, n, d, tag, attrs, Prepend(v, acc), stack)
                    Case Else
                        XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, Reverse(acc)), i)

Rem Is there a start tag at i, rather than a stray < or a comment?
Def HStartsElem(s As String, i As Number) As Boolean
    Mid(s, i, 1) = "<" And XIsNameStart(Mid(s, i + 1, 1))

Def HTagAt(s As String, i As Number) As String
    Lower(Mid(s, i + 1, HAttrNameEnd(s, i + 1) - i - 1))

Rem One node. A stray < that begins nothing is text, which is the single
Rem most common thing wrong with a hand-written page.
Def HNodeAt(s As String, i As Number, d As Number, stack As List Of String) As XTake
    If Mid(s, i, 1) <> "<" Then
        HTextAt(s, i)
    Else
        If Mid(s, i, 4) = "<!--" Then
            XCommentAt(s, i)
        Else
            If Mid(s, i, 9) = "<![CDATA[" Then
                XCDataAt(s, i)
            Else
                If Lower(Mid(s, i, 9)) = "<!doctype" Then
                    HDoctypeAt(s, i)
                Else
                    If Mid(s, i, 2) = "<?" Then
                        XPIAt(s, i)
                    Else
                        If HStartsElem(s, i) Then
                            HElemAt(s, i, d, stack)
                        Else
                            XTook(XText("<"), i + 1)

Rem The doctype, whole and unread, as xml does it — but HTML spells the
Rem keyword in any case, so the slice is taken by length rather than by
Rem matching.
Def HDoctypeAt(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    Let e = XInstrFrom(s, i + 9, ">")
    If e = 0 Then
        XTook(XDoctype(Mid(s, i + 9, Len(s) - i - 8)), Len(s) + 1)
    Else
        XTook(XDoctype(Mid(s, i + 9, e - i - 9)), e + 1)

Rem ---- the document ----------------------------------------------------
Rem Anything may appear at the top level and a page may have more than
Rem one root, so unlike xml this loop counts nothing and refuses nothing.
Rem A stray end tag with no open element is dropped, exactly as a browser
Rem drops it.

Def HDocNodes(s As String, i As Number, d As Number, acc As List Of Xml) As XRead
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XOk(XDocument(Reverse(acc)))
    Else
        If Mid(s, i, 2) = "</" Then
            Let g = XInstrFrom(s, i, ">")
            If g = 0 Then
                XOk(XDocument(Reverse(acc)))
            Else
                HDocNodes(s, g + 1, d, acc)
        Else
            Select Case HNodeAt(s, i, d, { })
                Case XTBad(why, at)
                    XErr(why, at)
                Case XTook(v, n)
                    If n <= i Then
                        XOk(XDocument(Reverse(acc)))
                    Else
                        HDocNodes(s, n, d, Prepend(v, acc))
                Case Else
                    XOk(XDocument(Reverse(acc)))

Rem ---- the public reader -----------------------------------------------
Rem HtmlRead is total for the same reason XmlRead is, but it has far less
Rem to say: the only thing that stops it is the depth budget.

Def HtmlReadDepth(s As String, maxDepth As Number) As XRead
    HDocNodes(s, 1, maxDepth, { })

Def HtmlRead(s As String) As XRead
    HtmlReadDepth(s, XmlMaxDepth())

Def HtmlParse(s As String) As Xml
    Select Case HtmlRead(s)
        Case XOk(v)
            v
        Case XErr(why, at)
            Error("HTMLPARSE: " & why & " AT " & Str(at))
        Case Else
            Error("HTMLPARSE: UNREACHABLE")

Def HtmlLoad(path As String) As Xml
    HtmlParse(ReadFile(path))

Rem ======================================================================
Rem THE WRITER
Rem ======================================================================
Rem Not xml's writer. A void element goes out bare, a raw-text element's
Rem content goes out unescaped, and an empty non-void element goes out as
Rem a pair — <div></div>, never <div/>, which browsers read as an open
Rem div and would swallow the rest of the page.

Def HtmlText(x As Xml) As String
    Join(Reverse(HFrags(x, { })), "")

Def HFrags(x As Xml, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    Select Case x
        Case XDocument(ns)
            HFragList(ns, acc)
        Case XText(t)
            Prepend(HtmlEscape(t), acc)
        Case XComment(b)
            Prepend("-->", Prepend(b, Prepend("<!--", acc)))
        Case XCData(r)
            Prepend("]]>", Prepend(r, Prepend("<![CDATA[", acc)))
        Case XDoctype(dtd)
            Prepend(">", Prepend(dtd, Prepend("<!DOCTYPE", acc)))
        Case XPI(t, dat)
            Prepend("?>", Prepend(dat, Prepend(" ", Prepend(t, Prepend("<?", acc)))))
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            If HIsVoid(tag) Then
                Prepend(">", XFragAttrs(attrs, Prepend(tag, Prepend("<", acc))))
            Else
                If HIsRawText(tag) Then
                    XFragClose(tag, Prepend(XTextOf(x), XFragOpen(tag, attrs, acc)))
                Else
                    XFragClose(tag, HFragList(kids, XFragOpen(tag, attrs, acc)))

Def HFragList(xs As List Of Xml, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        acc
    Else
        HFragList(Rest(xs), HFrags(First(xs), acc))

Def HtmlSave(path As String, x As Xml)
    WriteFile(path, HtmlText(x))

Rem ---- escaping --------------------------------------------------------
Rem & and < always. > as well, for the same reason xml escapes it. NOT
Rem the non-ASCII characters the entity table can name: a page that
Rem arrived as UTF-8 should leave as UTF-8, and turning an em dash back
Rem into &mdash; would make the writer's output depend on a table whose
Rem whole point is that it is incomplete.

Def HtmlEscape(s As String) As String
    XmlEscape(s)

Def HtmlEscapeAttr(s As String) As String
    XmlEscapeAttr(s)

Rem Turn the references in a string into the text they stand for, by
Rem HTML's rules — an unknown name stays as it is.
Def HtmlUnescape(s As String) As String
    Join(Reverse(HUnFrags(s, 1, 1, { })), "")

Def HUnFrags(s As String, i As Number, run As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XRun(s, run, i, acc)
    Else
        If Mid(s, i, 1) = "&" And HEntLen(s, i) > 0 Then
            HUnFrags(s, i + HEntLen(s, i), i + HEntLen(s, i), Prepend(HEntText(Mid(s, i + 1, HEntLen(s, i) - 2)), XRun(s, run, i, acc)))
        Else
            HUnFrags(s, i + 1, run, acc)

Rem ---- pretty ----------------------------------------------------------
Rem xml's rule, with one addition: a raw-text element is never
Rem re-indented, because its content is a program.

Def HtmlPretty(x As Xml, indent As Number) As String
    If indent <= 0 Then
        HtmlText(x)
    Else
        Select Case x
            Case XDocument(ns)
                Join(Reverse(HPFrags(x, indent, 0, { })), "") & XNl()
            Case Else
                Join(Reverse(HPFrags(x, indent, 0, { })), "")

Def HPFrags(x As Xml, indent As Number, level As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    Select Case x
        Case XDocument(ns)
            HPDoc(ns, indent, acc, True)
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            If IsEmpty(kids) Or XMixed(kids) Or HIsRawText(tag) Then
                HFrags(x, acc)
            Else
                XFragClose(tag, Prepend(XPad(indent, level), Prepend(XNl(), HPKids(Filter(kids, Fn(k) => Not XIsLayout(k)), indent, level + 1, XFragOpen(tag, attrs, acc)))))
        Case Else
            HFrags(x, acc)

Def HPDoc(ns As List Of Xml, indent As Number, acc As List Of String, lead As Boolean) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(ns) Then
        acc
    Else
        If XIsLayout(First(ns)) Then
            HPDoc(Rest(ns), indent, acc, lead)
        Else
            If lead Then
                HPDoc(Rest(ns), indent, HPFrags(First(ns), indent, 0, acc), False)
            Else
                HPDoc(Rest(ns), indent, HPFrags(First(ns), indent, 0, Prepend(XNl(), acc)), False)

Def HPKids(xs As List Of Xml, indent As Number, level As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        acc
    Else
        HPKids(Rest(xs), indent, level, HPFrags(First(xs), indent, level, Prepend(XPad(indent, level), Prepend(XNl(), acc))))

Rem ======================================================================
Rem FINDING THINGS
Rem ======================================================================
Rem Everything xml can do — XFind, XFindAll, XPath, XTextOf, XAttrOr,
Rem XEqual — works on a parsed page unchanged. These are the four
Rem questions that are specifically about HTML.

Rem Every element carrying this id, which should be one and is worth
Rem checking when it is not.
Def HAllById(x As Xml, id As String) As List Of Xml
    Filter(XDescend(x, { }), Fn(k) => XAttrOr(k, "id", "") = id)

Def HById(x As Xml, id As String) As Xml
    If IsEmpty(HAllById(x, id)) Then
        Error("HBYID: NO ELEMENT WITH id='" & id & "'")
    Else
        First(HAllById(x, id))

Def HByIdOr(x As Xml, id As String, dflt As Xml) As Xml
    If IsEmpty(HAllById(x, id)) Then
        dflt
    Else
        First(HAllById(x, id))

Rem The class attribute is a space-separated list, so this is membership
Rem rather than equality: class="mast has-icon" is found by either name.
Def HByClass(x As Xml, cls As String) As List Of Xml
    Filter(XDescend(x, { }), Fn(k) => Contains(Split(XAttrOr(k, "class", ""), " "), cls))

Def HByTag(x As Xml, tag As String) As List Of Xml
    XFindAll(x, Lower(tag))

Rem Every href an <a> carries, in document order, including the empty
Rem ones — a bare <a href=""> is worth seeing, not worth hiding.
Def HLinks(x As Xml) As List Of String
    Map(Filter(HByTag(x, "a"), Fn(k) => XHasAttr(k, "href")), Fn(k) => XAttr(k, "href"))

Rem Every src an <img> carries.
Def HImages(x As Xml) As List Of String
    Map(Filter(HByTag(x, "img"), Fn(k) => XHasAttr(k, "src")), Fn(k) => XAttr(k, "src"))

Rem Every id in the document, in document order. Duplicates are left in,
Rem because finding them is the reason to ask.
Def HIds(x As Xml) As List Of String
    Map(Filter(XDescend(x, { }), Fn(k) => XHasAttr(k, "id")), Fn(k) => XAttr(k, "id"))

Def HTitle(x As Xml) As String
    XTextOf(XFind(x, "title"))

Def HTitleOr(x As Xml, dflt As String) As String
    XTextOf(XFindOr(x, "title", XLeaf("title", dflt)))

Rem The visible text: what is left after the script and the style are
Rem taken out. Not what a browser would lay out — no collapsing of
Rem whitespace, no line boxes — but the text that is actually readable
Rem rather than the text that happens to be in the file.
Def HtmlTextOf(x As Xml) As String
    Join(Reverse(HVisFrags(x, { })), "")

Def HVisFrags(x As Xml, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    Select Case x
        Case XText(t)
            Prepend(t, acc)
        Case XCData(r)
            Prepend(r, acc)
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            If HIsRawText(tag) Then
                acc
            Else
                HVisList(kids, acc)
        Case XDocument(ns)
            HVisList(ns, acc)
        Case Else
            acc

Def HVisList(xs As List Of Xml, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        acc
    Else
        HVisList(Rest(xs), HVisFrags(First(xs), acc))
